  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request aroha_ngata turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: Aroha: "Don't just stand there — you've got opinions, right?"
    NPC: "Walk with me? I want another pair of eyes on something."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: "I buried this before the Scattering. Seemed stupid to keep it secret." Aroha digs up a wrapped bundle — food, still good. (+1990 kcal to the pantry.)
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "You look handy. What did you do with your hands, before?"
    YOU: (tell them your trade)
    NPC: "Useful. Everything useful matters now. I mean that as a compliment."
    YOU: "Take your time. I've got nowhere to be."
    NPC: "These hands? Comic shop owner hands. Clipboards, mostly. Now they hold wire and wood, and they learn fast. Hands are honest that way."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on what you did with your hands."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on what you did with your hands."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on what you did with your hands. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "I'll keep it to myself. What's on your mind?"
    YOU: "What's weighing on you right now?"
    NPC: "You asked me that before. It's a different question now." "Impress Us. They just... took you. Came back like nothing happened. It wasn't nothing."
    YOU: "What happened next?"
    NPC: "I wish we had longer. Soon, yeah?"
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You say nothing. Neither do they, for a while — and it's fine.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Good — what's been happening, settled. Feels better said out loud."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

