  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_ew19o49 turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Never mind this wound — we got it handled. Thanks anyway."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "Anyway — that's my problem, not yours. What did you want?"
    YOU: "Anything on your mind lately?"
    NPC: "You asked me that before. It's a different question now." "They say the table's coming. For us. I keep thinking about what we'd even bring to it."
    YOU: "Keep going."
    NPC: Whatever warmth was building cools to politeness.
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Someone has to answer it eventually. Everyone's doing the math on whether it'll be them."
    YOU: "Tell me more."
    NPC: "I clean up other people's messes quietly and practice what I'd say. In case it ever asks me. It won't. Still."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "I wish there was more to tell. That's it."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "Right — go on, I'm listening."
    YOU: "Be straight with me. What am I to you?"
    NPC: "Good question." "You're one of the good ones. Don't make me regret saying that out loud." "That's where we are."
    YOU: "I want to understand."
    NPC: A warmth settles over the conversation — they lean in a little.
    YOU: "I want to understand."
    NPC: "I've got things to see to. Don't be a stranger."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "It's been a while. Glad we circled back to what's been happening."
    NPC: "This was good." They mean it.

